s. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,security,readers,groups\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/security/security/init.rs check_security, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"check_security's group loop passes when the library readers contain 'anonymous' OR the caller's group, so library=anonymous plus per-command groups is the fine-grained convention; check_auth (app.read/write/delete and app.exec-by-id) has NO anonymous pass-through - the group must appear in BOTH the library readers and the record readers, so group-gating a control's records for non-admin readers also requires that group at the library level.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Verified live: /dev/lib_info gated to 'testers' executed for a testers user and denied anonymous/other; app.read of a testers-gated control in the anonymous-readers dev library denied the testers user (admin passed). Command::new reads readers from the command META record, not the impl record.\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,check_security,check_auth,enforcement\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390471\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Command exposure model (check_security): with security on, a command executes anonymously only if BOTH the library meta's readers and the command record's readers contain 'anonymous'; otherwise the session user's groups must intersect the command's readers, and the 'admin' group always passes. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,security,readers,groups\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbou