ntegration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390471\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"An uninstalled library fails closed and clearly: check_auth and check_security return false when system.libraries lacks the lib, and app.read/app.exec answer {status:err, msg:'NO SUCH LIBRARY: <lib>'} before auth - previously a read/exec against a missing lib (the agent add-on on a plain install) panicked in check_auth with ndata's cryptic \\\"Key 'agent' not found\\\".\",\n    \"detail\": \"Verified on a disposable with security=on: /app/read?lib=agent&id=controls and /app/exec?lib=agent answer the clean err envelope with zero panics in the log; anonymous read of dev/controls unaffected. Bench side: the dev.dev boot filters its [lib, app, agent] controls-index sweep through /app/libs first, and app.store's controls() checks the cached library list before any wire call, so store.invoke/agentLibCall against an absent agent answer 'library \\\"agent\\\" is not installed on this instance' without touching the server. Gotcha found en route: config.properties security expects the string 'on'/'off' - security=true parses as OFF (flowlang appserver.rs ~236/256).\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,check_auth,check_security,missing-library,agent-optional,bench,plugin\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (newbound: security.security.init, app.app.read, app.app.exec, dev.dev js, app.store js)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786365273284\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Command exposure model (check_security): with security on, a command executes anonymously only if BOTH the library meta's readers and the command record's readers contain 'anonymous'; otherwise the session user's groups must intersect the command's readers, and the 'admin' group always passes. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the 